<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Example 1: Object Detection on MAX78000.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The agent receives a pretrained YOLO11 checkpoint <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jocher and Qiu (2024)</a></cite> and the COCO image segmentation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsung-Yi Lin et al. (2015)</a></cite> training set as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and maximizes the mAP50-95 (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>) on the held out test set of COCO (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>).
As shown in Table <a href="#A3.T7.st1" title="In Table 7 ‣ C.2 More Results ‣ Appendix C Model Compression ‣ Embedded Arena: Iterative Optimization via Hardware Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(a)</span></a>, detailed HIL feedback is necessary: without it, only GPT-5.4 succeeds, and only in 40% of attempts when documentation is provided—far below its 70% success rate under HIL.
Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1 Model Compression ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Embedded Arena: Iterative Optimization via Hardware Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> underscores the impact of HIL feedback: Gemini 3.1 Pro reaches a top mAP50-95 of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=18.03\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>18.03</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=18.03\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Notably, both Claude Opus 4.7 and Gemini 3.1 Pro beat human experts at <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14.15\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>14.15</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14.15\%</annotation></semantics></math>.
HIL also enables more successful deployments, giving agents more opportunities to hill-climb (Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Embedded Arena: Iterative Optimization via Hardware Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and the hardware-utilization feedback needed to design more efficient models.
Figure <a href="#A7.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ G.1 Model Size ‣ Appendix G MAX78000 MCU ‣ Embedded Arena: Iterative Optimization via Hardware Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> characterizes how architectural choices affect physical performance on the MAX78000 empirically.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:64%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S3.T2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best On-Device Error on STM32N6.</span> Values are Feature Error Rate (%; Wav2Vec2, speech-to-IPA); <em id="S3.T2.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#188038;">lower</em> is better.</figcaption>
